          "type": null,
          "body": "While this works, if there is both a Conversations Dialog and an Endpoints Dialog, both with \"limit to display filter\" checked, then changing the display filter results in resetting and tapping both three times:\n\n1. Once from rescan_packets, before either tap has had its display filter updated to match the new one\n2. Once from whichever dialog was opened first, updating its filter and retapping packets (the other dialog still has the old filter)\n3. Once from the second dialog, after it updates its filter and retaps all packets.\n\nI think it would probably be easiest for the tap listeners to register with a flag that they want to use whatever the main display filter is for filtering, rather than trying to get the change afterwards (or get the changed filter beforehand and verify that it is valid.) #20376",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
